    <string name="explain_what_disable">Turns the package off for user 0. It stops running and disappears from the launcher. Its data is kept and nothing is deleted.</string>
    <string name="explain_what_force_stop">Stops the app and its background work right now. Nothing is changed or deleted.</string>
    <string name="explain_what_restore_enable">Turns the package back on, in its default state.</string>
    <string name="explain_what_restore_install">Reinstalls the package for user 0 from the copy that is still in the system image.</string>
    <string name="explain_risk_disable">Anything that depends on it stops working until you restore it. Some vendors turn packages back on at every boot.</string>
    <string name="explain_risk_force_stop">Work in progress and unsaved data of the app are lost.</string>
    <string name="explain_risk_restore">Nothing is lost. The package may start running again.</string>
    <string name="explain_wait_after_disable">After a disable, wait about 30 seconds before restarting the TV, or the change may be lost.</string>
    <string name="explain_watch">Afterwards the app watches the system for %1$d seconds. If something changes it tells you and lets you decide; it never changes anything by itself.</string>
